  "modules": [
    {
      "id": "uniequip_001_texas",
      "name": {
        "en": "Texas's Badge",
        "zh": "德克萨斯证章",
        "source": "official",
        "isMachineTranslation": false
      },
      "type": "INITIAL",
      "typeName2": "",
      "icon": "uniequip_001_texas",
      "description": {
        "en": "Operator Texas has demonstrated a remarkable aptitude for preemptive penetration of the battlefield situation and active offense so as to secure leeway for deployment.\nThe Field Operations Department has thus passed the following resolution:\nThis operator shall hereby be appointed a Vanguard Operator during field operations to exercise Pioneer responsibilities.\nIn witness whereof,\nThis badge is hereby conferred upon the above named.",
        "zh": "干员德克萨斯擅长抢先切入战局，通过进攻争取部署空间\n根据外勤部门决议\n在外勤任务中划分为先锋干员，行使尖兵职责\n特别颁发此证章\n以兹证明",
        "source": "official",
        "isMachineTranslation": false
      },
      "servers": [
        "cn",
        "global"
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "uniequip_002_texas",
      "name": {
        "en": "Private Field Supply Package",
        "zh": "外勤私人补给包",
        "source": "official",
        "isMachineTranslation": false
      },
      "type": "ADVANCED",
      "typeName2": "Y",
      "icon": "uniequip_002_texas",
      "description": {
        "en": "Lungmen Guard Department/Transcript:\n'Yes, Ah Sir, I remember clearly, it was a young Lupo lady, black hair and orange eyes, carrying a briefcase. Her name's Texas, you said? I've never heard it. I keep to myself, you know.'\n'What happened? Everything was normal, I was there at the counter spacing out. A little shop like ours doesn't do much business at three in the afternoon. Students are still in school, and the office types come by at noon to stretch their limbs for a bit before their bosses pull them back to work. I suppose officers like you on patrol mind our business now and again. Do you know Madame Oni? The tall, tall Inspector with a horn on her head? She and I—'\n'Black suits! Er, I was a little nervous, there must've been twenty in all. Us ordinary folks never see things like that. They were all rushing Miss Texas and that briefcase, and whatever they had in their hands, they were shiny and glinting! You see something like that for real, I dare say, and it makes those movies look like child's play! You know, Ah Sir, I'm a professional, I've seen every kung fu movie to ever come out in Lungmen, but the way Miss Texas squared up was completely different. She doesn't even seem that old. I don't dare imagine where she learned those insane moves, or how she got so trained.'\n'Right, the camera has me hiding under the counter, but I heard it all crystal clear! A dagger got sent flying and landed right next to me! Then a red-haired Sankta came in, I think probably to help Miss Texas, because I heard them say hi. She was called Exusiai? And then there was this whole massive rumble, that was something wild! I could feel my own liver shaking!'\n'Then it all died down, and I found the guts to come out from under the counter, and the black suits were all on the ground, and my shop was—ah, you don't have to worry about that, there were two big stars who came by later on. Miss Sora was one, and then the other was that rapping Liberi. They compensated me wonderfully, enough I could fix up my shop and open a cystybeast meatball stall.'\n'What about Texas? Er, she... she picked out some snacks after it went down and went to me to pay. It was the kind that's really popular with schoolkids, the biscuit sticks with the coating. She bought a whole handful of boxes. Chocolate, vanilla and the new salted one, and she bought a woven bag for a dollar too.'\n'What do you mean, I'm not telling you anything useful? You listen to me, that bag is designed by our shop! It's got cartoons on it!'\n'Alright, enough from me. Still, Ah Sir, there's one more thing—do you L.G.D. people know this Miss Texas? Tell her for me: the reward from her stamp card came in, a limited edition baseball cap, so if she can drop in when she's got the time...'\nNote by personnel on shift: Filed under Folder-Penguin Logistics 1097 (102), all charges on incident provisionally dropped.",
        "zh": "龙门近卫局/笔录：\n“是，阿sir，我看得很清楚，那是个鲁珀姑娘，黑头发橙色眼睛，拎着个公文包。你说她叫德克萨斯？我没听过这个名字，我可是本分人。”\n“当时的情况？当时我就和平常一样，在柜台那发呆。像我们这种小超市，下午三点可做不成什么生意，学生们还没放学，那帮坐办公室的中午会过来放风，下午都被老板捉走继续上工啦，倒是你们这些巡逻的警员，偶尔会来照顾我们生意。你认识鬼姐吗？头上长角，个子高高的督察，她和我——”\n“黑衣人！呃，是有点夸张，二十个总还是有的。我们小老百姓可从来没见过这种场面。那帮人冲着德克萨斯小姐和那只公文包就去了，手上可都亮着明晃晃的家伙呢！那场面，我敢说，见过真格的以后，那些电影就成了哄小孩的玩意啦！阿sir，我可是专业的，龙门所有的武打片我都看过，德克萨斯小姐的架势可不一样，我都不敢想，她看起来年纪也不大，到底是从哪里学来这些鬼招式，又怎么会用得这么熟练的。”\n“是，监控里我是躲在柜台底下呢，可我听得真切啊！有把被打飞的匕首就落在我旁边！后来又来了个红头发的萨科塔，应该是来给德克萨斯小姐帮忙的，听她们称呼，好像叫能天使？然后就是轰隆隆一顿乱炸，那可真够意思，我心肝儿都在颤！”\n“后来没声了，我就大着胆子从柜台下面出来了，穿黑衣服的全躺啦，我的小超市也——啊，这你倒不用担心，后来来了两个大明星，一个是空小姐，还有一个是那个搞说唱的黎博利，他们的赔偿给得很大方，够我修了超市再开个瘤兽丸子档口的。”\n“你问德克萨斯？呃，她……她之后拿了些零食找我结账，就是那种学生里很流行的，裹了酱的饼干棒。她买了好几盒，巧克力味，香草味还有新款的盐味，还要了个一块钱的编织袋。”\n“什么叫我光说没用的？那可是我们超市特别设计的编织袋！有卡通图案的！”\n“好吧，我不说了。不过，阿sir，还有件小事——这位德克萨斯小姐和你们近卫局很熟吗？帮我带个话：她的零食集点卡奖品到了，限量版的棒球帽，请她有空来……”\n当值警员批注：已归档卷宗-企鹅物流1097（102），本事件暂不追责。",
        "source": "official",
        "isMachineTranslation": false
      },
